A||||2||Taijiguy||Where to buy building supplies:||||14||
Z||000000||Taijiguy||09-17-2001||11:12 PM||||Locally, a group of people who initially wanted to go lend assistance were discouraged, since they didn't really have any rescue or recovery skills or experience. So instead, they went around to gather items needed by the rescue workers, and deliver them to New York. When they approached other stores, they were turned away stating that donations had been made at the corporate level. When they approached Lowes, the store manager without hesitation gave them permission to take anything that was needed. To "clear the shelves" if necessary. The people were given assistance by several employees, who went from one end of the store to the other, and gathered all of the best of everything, gloves, masks, various tools and implements, to aid in the operation. They did in fact clear the shelves of many items. This generosity was extended, despite the fact that on a corporate level, Lowes donated about $1,000,000 to the efforts. Just another example of how people are pulling together for a common goal. ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cheever3000||09-17-2001||11:31 PM||||That's awesome.  I'm going to remember that.  Lowe's is only a little farther from me than the "orange box", so I think I know where I'll be shopping in the future.  And I'll be sure to tell them why.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||09-18-2001||07:46 PM||||we don't have any Lowes stores here..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> we have all the other big ones though.. home depot, ace, etc..<P>but if we did, I'd probably give them some extra business because of that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
